messages:
sara: Quick check — I'm planning a small terraform change to reduce replicas for statefulset 'kv-store' from 3 -> 2 during a low-traffic window. Wanted to run through safety checklist. TL;DR: will we risk losing quorum? cc @mike

mike: Probably fine if we ensure pod ordinals preserve leader placement. What are we changing in TF? link to diff? :eyes:

sara: Here's the diff I'm going to apply: `module.kv.k8s_statefulset.replicas = 2` — actual HCL snippet in the module: ```hcl
resource "kubernetes_stateful_set" "kv" {
  metadata { name = "kv-store" }
  spec {
    replicas = var.kv_replicas
    service_name = "kv-svc"
    ...
  }
}
```
Will update var in vars.tfvars and run `terraform plan` first.

dan: If it's a DB that relies on ordinal ordering it's risky. Do we have a PodDisruptionBudget? Also ensure PV retention - we shouldn't recreate PVCs. Also check topologySpreadConstraints and anti-affinity.

emma: Add a canary: scale down one replica in staging first, watch recovery. Also bump readinessProbe timeout by 10s during rollout so we don't get flapping.

sara: Good call. Plan: 1) update var and run plan in staging, 2) apply in staging and monitor for 30m, 3) apply in prod during 02:00-04:00 UTC window, 4) if any failing pods, revert var to 3. Thoughts?

mike: @dan can you confirm PDB allows 1 unavailable? Our PDB currently minAvailable=2 which would block `replicas=2` for a 3-rep cluster. If so we need to adjust or remove PDB temporarily.

dan: Checked: PDB currently has `minAvailable = 2`. For replicas=2 you'd need `minAvailable = 1` (or switch to `maxUnavailable = 1`). Prefer changing PDB to minAvailable: 1 for the window. Remember to restore after.

sara: I'll include the PDB change in the same TF change set. Proposed code: ```hcl
resource "kubernetes_pod_disruption_budget" "kv_pdb" {
  metadata { name = "kv-pdb" }
  spec {
    min_available = 1
  }
}
``` — will add a TODO to revert to 2 after the window.

infra-bot: Deploy preview for branch `sara/kv-replicas` -> https://deploys.redwood.io/preview/kv/1769876543 (plan shows replacement of PDB and update of replicas).

mike: :thumbsup: After staging run, ping me and I'll do the prod apply. Also consider adding `lifecycle { ignore_changes = ["spec.template.metadata.annotations"] }` on the sts to avoid spur rollouts from annotations. Not mandatory.

sara: Noting lifecycle ignore change for annotation updates to avoid unnecessary rollouts — I'll leave as a comment in the PR. Test plan: `kubectl get pods -l app=kv -w` and watch leader election logs: `kubectl logs $(kubectl get pods -l app=kv -o name | head -n1)`

emma: If you hit unexpected leader loss, escalate to oncall. Also add a post-apply smoke check that verifies kv-ping latency < 50ms (CI job).

sara: Thanks all. I'll open the PR now and tag reviewers @mike @dan @emma. Scheduling prod apply for 2026-03-18 02:30 UTC unless objections.

mike: No objections. :shipit:
